(4) _Acceptance-rejection method:_ 1) Generate a pair of uniform deviates (\(U_{1},\ U_{2}\)); 2) compute \(z\) = - \(\ln\,u_{1}\); 3) if \(e^{- 1/2}(\mp u_{2})\leq u_{2}\) (or equivalently \((x - 1)^{2} \geq - 2\left( \ln\,u_{2} \right)\) accept \(z\), otherwise reject the pair and start over. The quantity will be the required normal deviate with mean zero and unit variance.

**b. Bivariate normal distribution**

Let \(\left\{ X_{1},\ X_{2}\right\}\) be a pair of independent normal deviates with mean zero and unit variance. Then \(\left\{ X_{1},\,\rho X_{1} + \left( {1 - \rho} \right)^{1/2}X_{2}\right\}\) represent a pair of deviates from a bivariate normal distribution with zero means, unit variances, and correlation coefficient \(\rho\).

**c. Exponential distribution**

